# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALLOW-LIST .gitignore (critique CRITICAL: a block-list always misses something
# in this kind of repo — keychain comments, agent-card org, second PHI copy).
# Strategy: ignore EVERYTHING first, then re-allow only the portable surface.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything.
*

# 2) Re-allow the portable directories (and let their contents be matched below).
!/council/
!/constitution/
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/tests/
!/.github/
!*/

# 3) Re-allow only safe, portable file types.
!*.md
!*.py
!*.toml
!*.txt
!*.sh
!*.ps1
!*.rb
!*.json
!*.sql
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!*.cff
!*.svg
!*.png
!*.editorconfig
!*.gitattributes
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# 4) NEVER commit these machine-specific leaks, even if a rule above re-allowed them.
council.local.*
# ...but the tracked, secret-free example template IS committed (no inline comments in gitignore)
!council.local.example.toml
COUNCIL.md
COUNCIL.local.md
KONSEY_ANAYASASI.md
KONSEY_ANAYASASI_*archived*
KONSEY_ANAYASASI_GENEL*.md
KONSEY_LESSONS.md
a2a_peers.json
council/a2a/agent-card.json
bin/konsey-keychain.sh
# orchestrator's private work journal (absolute paths, real org names) — this repo's own
# provenance/decision record lives in CHANGELOG.md + KONSEY_ANAYASASI.md instead (2026-08-03,
# found one already-committed leak: CP-20260711-0100-parallel-plan-rank-faz1.md, untracked below)
/.prometheus/

# 5) Runtime / data / secrets — never tracked.
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
backups/
logs/
sessions/
recall-cache.json
**/.captured.log
**/.processing
dashboard.html
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# 6) Build / venv / caches.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
